<PageTitle>About | Miss Mary's Little Lambs</PageTitle>
<article class="information-page">
    <h1>Meet Miss Mary</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">Nurturing little hearts. Inspiring big learning.</p>
    <img class="about-photo" src="images/miss-mary.jpg" alt="Miss Mary and her daughter" />
    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p>Hi, I’m Miss Mary—an educator who teaches with intention, patience, and heart. I believe children learn best when they feel calm, safe, and genuinely excited about learning. At Miss Mary’s Little Lambs Homeschool, I create a peaceful, nurturing environment where children are free to be their authentic selves while developing a true love for learning.</p>
    <h2>My Journey Into Teaching</h2>
    <p>I have been an elementary school teacher since 2018. I earned my Bachelor of Science in Education in 2015 and my Master of Science in Education in 2021. Teaching has always been more than a career for me—it is a calling rooted in my lifelong love for children and learning.</p>
    <p>With 8 years of classroom experience and a deep love for children, I create a calm, nurturing environment where learning feels joyful and meaningful.</p>
    <p>Becoming a mother to my daughter deepened my calling. As a new mom, I felt a strong desire to be present for her while continuing to do the work I am most passionate about. Opening my preschool allows me to blend motherhood and education in a way that feels purposeful, meaningful, and aligns with my values.</p>
</article>
